    "created_at": "2020-11-29T01:53:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-11-29T01:53:45Z",
    "body": "So unfortunately, there's a pretty major snag with this, which is that at least bash (and I suspect Nu, Ion, and possibly powershell) doesn't let you easily access the command that was last entered. That is, from starship, we have no way of accessing what the last command was, hence no way of telling what command was run.\r\n\r\nIf we ever want to do reactive modules the way pl10k does it, we'll need to work out some way around that, which we could then hook this type of feature into, but that's at least a year out (possibly more).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
